  ('cabo-pulmo-mexico', '10S', 'Cabo Pulmo', 'Mexico', 'The Sea of Cortez, recovered', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"expedition","diveglobal"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Federally protected National Marine Park since June 5, 1995; ~71 km2 fully protected (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabo_Pulmo_National_Park, 2026-07-04)","463% total fish-biomass increase, ~11x top-predator jump by 2009 — most successful no-take recovery measured (Source: ocean.si.edu, 2026-07-04)","Only living hard-coral reef in the Sea of Cortez; UNESCO WHS 2005, Ramsar 2008 (Source: en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04)","CONANP no-take rules: guide-led 6:1, no touching, gloves banned, licensed pangas only (Source: mexicotraveladventure.com, 2026-07-04)","Off-grid village; ~2-3 h drive north of SJD / Los Cabos; eco-cabañas only, no luxury hotels (Source: sallysees.com, 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_trauma":"Cabo San Lucas / San Jose del Cabo (Los Cabos), ~2-3 h by road; La Paz alternative","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"Baja California Sur US Level 2 (Exercise Increased Caution), May 29, 2026 — freely bookable, disclose L2, no hold","malaria":"none","dengue":"present in Baja California Sur; use repellent","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"May 15-Nov 30, peak Aug-Oct","remote_medevac":"off-grid; no chamber/hospital in village; multi-hour ground evac to Los Cabos","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jul-Nov (best visibility, bull-shark aggregation)","shoulder":"Apr-Jun, late fall","green":"Dec-Feb (coolest water, wind days)","booking_window_lead_time":"2-4 months (capped dive slots + tiny bed inventory)","out_of_season_fill":"winter dive-and-stay packages; East Cape / Los Cabos day-trip combos","holiday_event_peaks":["US/Canada summer holidays","Los Cabos Dec-Apr high-season spillover"],"campaign_start_trigger":"late spring for summer-fall dive peak; Los Cabos winter high season for day-trip capture"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Pulmo reef recovery dive","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Bull-shark aggregation dive","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator + DMC","name":"Protected-reef snorkel","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Sea-lion / offshore pinnacle dives","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"operator; stay direct","name":"Multi-day Cabo Pulmo dive-and-stay","si":"diveglobal"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Cabo Pulmo worth diving, and what will I see?","a":"Yes — it is arguably the Sea of Cortez''s best dive, because protection worked: total fish biomass rebounded 463% by 2009 on the Gulf''s only living hard-coral reef. Expect schooling jacks, groupers and rays, and in warm summer–fall water a bull-shark aggregation.","source":"ocean.si.edu / divearoo.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Do I need to be certified, and can non-divers go?","a":"You dive within your card with a mandatory park guide (max 6 divers each), and non-divers can snorkel the same no-take reef. The rules are strict — no gloves, no touching, licensed pangas only — and enforced; break them and you can be pulled from the water.","source":"mexicotraveladventure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can couples make a romantic escape of Cabo Pulmo?","a":"Only if \"romantic\" means off-grid and simple — there is no resort or spa layer. Lodging is solar eco-cabañas and a tiny villa cluster (~5 villas), which suits low-key couples; anyone wanting branded luxury bases in Los Cabos or the East Cape and day-trips in.","source":"sallysees.com / cabopulmo.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is diving here dangerous — what''s the real risk?","a":"The gatekeeper is medevac distance, not the diving itself. Cabo Pulmo is off-grid with no chamber or hospital in the village; the nearest recompression chamber and trauma care are ~2–3 hours away in Los Cabos, so dive conservatively, carry DAN cover, and observe 18–24 h no-fly before an SJD departure.","source":"sssnetwork.com / dan.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cabo Pulmo Diving — Sea of Cortez No-Take Reef | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Dive Cabo Pulmo, the most-recovered no-take marine reserve in the Sea of Cortez. Guided park dives, no-touch rules, eco-cabaña stays, Los Cabos gateway logistics.","primary_keywords":["Cabo Pulmo diving","Cabo Pulmo National Park","Cabo Pulmo snorkeling","Sea of Cortez reef"],"long_tail":["best time to dive Cabo Pulmo","Cabo Pulmo bull shark season","how to get to Cabo Pulmo from Los Cabos","Cabo Pulmo eco cabañas"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["buceo Cabo Pulmo","Parque Nacional Cabo Pulmo","arrecife de coral Mar de Cortes","snorkel Cabo Pulmo","reserva marina sin pesca","cabanas ecologicas Cabo Pulmo"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","diveglobal"],"ultra":[{"what":"Four Seasons Los Cabos at Costa Palmas / Amanvari (East Cape, Los Cabos) as luxury base for a Cabo Pulmo dive charter","why_ultra":"largest swimmable beach + only private marina in Los Cabos; Amanvari is first Aman in Mexico (spring 2026)","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"resort credit, upgrade, breakfast; private guide for Pulmo run","mor":"resale via host-Virtuoso only; Cabo Pulmo itself is NOT an ultra stay — nearest ultra is Los Cabos"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cabo Pulmo, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":23.4433,"lng":-109.4283}}'::jsonb, 15),
