ength of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Mar (dry, cool; Dec-Feb sweet spot)","inflection":"early autumn demand build; Carnaval late-Feb micro-peak","fire_date":"mid-to-late September (curve-start minus 1-2 wks); +2nd fire ~2 wks pre-Carnaval","green_season":"Jun-Oct (rainy, hotter, value)","attach":"Merida / Yucatan circuit (~2.5 hr)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Walled centro — pastel streets & eight bastions","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/895/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided walking tour + boutique-hotel room commission (wall free)"},{"name":"Puerta de Tierra sound-and-light show","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","source":"https://campechecity.com/best-time-to-visit-campeche/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"bundle into guided evening; ticket non-commissionable pass-through"},{"name":"Fuerte de San Miguel — Museo Arqueológico de Campeche","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/attractions/museo-arqueologico-de-campeche-fuerte-de-san-miguel/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided half-day + transfer margin; entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Edzná Maya ruins (52 km SE)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.themayanruinswebsite.com/edzna.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided archaeology day tour (DMC/affiliate) + site fee pass-through"},{"name":"Xtacumbilxunaán caves (near Bolonchén)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/attractions/grutas-de-xtacumbilxunaan/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided day tour (commissionable) + entry pass-through"},{"name":"Isla Aguada / Isla del Carmen dolphin encounter","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en-yucatan.com/campeche/isla-aguada/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","si":"romance","blurb":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"licensed sanctuary boat tour via affiliate (GetYourGuide/Civitatis) or DMC"},{"name":"The Malecón at sunset (7 km Gulf-front)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"free amenity selling boutique-hotel package"},{"name":"Candlelit colonial-courtyard dining","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/cpehl-hacienda-puerta-campeche-a-luxury-collection-hotel-campeche/overview/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"hotel F&B + room commission"},{"name":"Pan de cazón (state dish)","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/lifestyle/food/state-by-plate-campeches-pan-de-cazon/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","si":"culinary","blurb":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided food walk / cooking class (tour affiliate)"},{"name":"Pámpano en escabeche & coctel campechano","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/campeche-food-guide/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"curated dining list + food tour / market visit"},{"name":"Calakmul gateway (own dossier)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"premier","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/895/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","si":"culture","blurb":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"multi-day DMC program from Campeche City"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is there to see in the walled city?","a":"The UNESCO centro itself: a 17th-century wall (1686–1704), eight bastions, a checkerboard grid and 1,000+ colonial buildings painted ochre, coral and mint — walk Calle 59 at golden hour. At night, the Puerta de Tierra sound-and-light show projects four centuries of pirate history onto the Land Gate for about US$5.","source":"whc.unesco.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Edzná worth a day trip from Campeche?","a":"Yes — it is the region''s under-visited Maya highlight. Edzná, 52 km southeast, is a major Maya capital whose five-story pyramid rises ~40 m and blends Puuc, Chenes and Petén styles, with a rare ancient hydraulic canal system and a fraction of Chichén Itzá''s crowds. Go at the 8 AM opening to beat the heat.","source":"themayanruinswebsite.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Campeche good for a couple''s trip?","a":"Yes, as a slow, characterful pause. Dinner in a restored-hacienda courtyard (La Guardia at Hacienda Puerta Campeche), a rooftop pool at an 18th-century mansion, and the peninsula''s best sunset along the 7-km malecón make it a honeymoon-adjacent \"second city,\" most often paired with Mérida (~2.5 hr) as a 2–3 night add-on.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What should I eat in Campeche?","a":"Start with pan de cazón — the state dish of layered tortillas, black beans, shredded dogfish and tomato-habanero sauce. Add pámpano en escabeche (colonial-era pompano in bitter-orange escabeche) and the coctel campechano seafood cocktail, with Gulf catch landed the same morning.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Campeche?","a":"Heat and thin flight schedules, not crime. The exposed ruins at Edzná and the treeless malecón are hot at midday — hat, high SPF, water and early site visits. Campeche''s own airport (CPE) is thinly served, so most travelers fly into Mérida (MID) and drive ~2.5 hr; drink bottled water only and use repellent for dengue in the rainy season (Jun–Oct).","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Campeche City, Mexico — The Walled UNESCO Pastel Port | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Campeche","ciudad amurallada Campeche","Edzná zona arqueológica","hoteles boutique centro histórico Campeche","avistamiento de delfines Isla Aguada","pan de cazón Campeche","Carnaval de Campeche fechas"],"long_tail_en":["is Campeche City Mexico safe","things to do in Campeche walled city","Edzná ruins day trip from Campeche","Isla Aguada dolphin tour Campeche","best boutique hotels Campeche historic center"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Campeche City"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hacienda Puerta Campeche, a Luxury Collection Hotel","brand":"Marriott — Luxury Collection","rooms":14,"positioning":"Restored 16th-c. haciendas; the destination''s true luxury ceiling","earning":"Marriott commissionable; Luxury Collection eligible for Marriott STARS/Luxury consortia — verify FHR/amenity status at booking","mor":"hotel-direct commission","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Casa Don Gustavo Boutique Hotel","rooms":10,"positioning":"Restored 18th-c. mansion, rooftop pool, pedestrian center","earning":"Independent — direct / bedbank / consortia","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"$$$"},{"property":"Hotel H177","positioning":"Boutique centro property, Calle 59","earning":"Independent boutique; direct / affiliate","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Campeche City, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.845,"lng":-90.523}}'::jsonb, 18),
