any organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season, polo/Ondalinda/celebrity winter season, holiday villa demand, humpbacks Dec-Mar)","shoulder":"May & late Oct (warm, quieter, between festivals)","green":"Jul-Oct (hot/humid, emerald hills, hurricane window May-Nov, softest villa availability)","event_peak":"polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter, Chinese New Year tournament); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","booking_window_lead_time":"staffed ultra villas for Christmas-New Year/winter polo/Ondalinda book 6-12 months ahead, contracted direct on application; binding constraint is villa availability, not flights","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green season (Jul-Oct) villa buyouts at softer rates as private-family estate stays (turtle nesting Cuixmala) - the ''secret season''","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year (ultra premium), Semana Santa/Easter (Agua Alta Cup polo), Chinese New Year (polo+gala), Ondalinda (mid-Nov)","campaign_start_trigger":"content-only - no campaign; if founder rules private-air carve-out, open winter/polo/Ondalinda villa campaigns in spring for following Nov-Apr peak (6-12-mo villa lead)","sources":["https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","https://careyes.com/","https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Careyes clifftop Castles","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"candy-colored castles with moat-like infinity pools cantilevered over the Pacific — the signature Careyes image","si":"ultra","blurb":"candy-colored castles with moat-like infinity pools cantilevered over the Pacific — the signature Careyes image","when":"year-round","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Cuixmala (Casa Cuixmala suites / hillside villas)","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Cuixmala direct / luxury DMC","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/mexico/cuixmala.html","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre biosphere estate — zebras, nesting turtles, private airstrip, total seclusion","si":"ultra","blurb":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre biosphere estate — zebras, nesting turtles, private airstrip, total seclusion","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Las Alamandas direct / DMC","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"18 suites across 8 villas, plus 16% VAT / 3% room tax / 14% service. On application","si":"ultra","blurb":"18 suites across 8 villas, plus 16% VAT / 3% room tax / 14% service. On application","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Careyes staffed-villa honeymoon","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"private staffed villa/casita with cook, cliff-and-cove privacy — a celebrity-wedding coast","si":"romance","blurb":"private staffed villa/casita with cook, cliff-and-cove privacy — a celebrity-wedding coast","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"El Careyes Club & Residences","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable":"Careyes reservations","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"beachfront club stay for couples wanting hotel-style service inside the enclave","si":"romance","blurb":"beachfront club stay for couples wanting hotel-style service inside the enclave","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Careyes polo - Agua Alta Cup (Easter)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"Careyes events / villa package","source":"https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the enclave''s signature spectacle, played Easter week; Chinese New Year tournament too","si":"ocean","blurb":"the enclave''s signature spectacle, played Easter week; Chinese New Year tournament too","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Sailing + winter humpback coast","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable":"charter / villa concierge (content-only)","source":"https://www.costalegre.ca/","hook":"sailing off the coves; humpbacks migrate Dec–Mar offshore","si":"ocean","blurb":"sailing off the coves; humpbacks migrate Dec–Mar offshore","commission":"operator (content-only)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book Careyes through TravelWell right now?","a":"No — Careyes is content-only today. Jalisco sits at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (May 29, 2026), and the advisory''s only named no-restriction carve-outs are the Guadalajara Metro area, Puerto Vallarta, Chapala and Ajijic — four zones that do not include Careyes. Failing that named-carve-out gate sets book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Careyes?","a":"The road transfer, not the enclave itself. Ground transfers from Puerto Vallarta or Manzanillo run through non-carve-out southern Jalisco, and the advisory warns specifically against secondary highways after dark — this is the hold reason. The enclave is also remote: serious medical cases route ~1.5 hr to Manzanillo or 2–4 hr to Puerto Vallarta, so air-evac insurance is essential.","source":"travel.state.gov / careyes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What makes Careyes so exclusive?","a":"It is a genuinely private, family-owned ultra node — not a resort. Founded in 1968, it pairs clifftop castles and ~50 staffed villas with two adjacent Goldsmith estates: Cuixmala, a ~25,000-acre biosphere reserve with its own airstrip, and Las Alamandas, an 18-suite gated boutique. All three have private airstrips — the crux of a possible future \"arrive-by-private-air\" clean pass.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com / careyes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ultra"},{"q":"Is Careyes good for a honeymoon or wedding?","a":"Yes — it is one of Mexico''s most cinematic private-wedding coasts. Heidi Klum and Seal married here, and the product is a fully staffed villa or casita with a private cook and total cliff-and-cove privacy, plus El Careyes Club & Residences for hotel-style service. Peak is the dry Nov–Apr season, and villas for that window contract 6–12 months ahead.","source":"careyes.com / aol.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is polo season and the Ondalinda festival?","a":"Professional polo runs late November to the end of April, with the marquee Agua Alta Cup played Easter week and a Chinese New Year tournament; the Ondalinda x Careyes festival is dated Nov 12–15, 2026. Winter also brings humpbacks offshore (Dec–Mar). Staffed-villa demand for these dates books 6–12 months out.","source":"ondalinda.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Careyes Mexico: Clifftop Castles, Polo & the Costalegre Ultra Coast","meta_description":"Careyes — Gian Franco Brignone''s 1968 private ultra enclave on Jalisco''s Costalegre: clifftop castles, staffed villas, polo, sailing, Ondalinda, plus Cuixmala & Las Alamandas.","slug":"careyes-mexico","primary_keyword":"Careyes Mexico","long_tail":["Careyes villas rent","Careyes clifftop castles","Careyes polo Agua Alta Cup","Ondalinda Careyes 2026","Cuixmala vs Careyes vs Las Alamandas","Careyes private airstrip access"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Careyes Mexico","villas Careyes renta","castillos Careyes","polo Careyes Copa Agua Alta","Ondalinda Careyes 2026","Cuixmala reserva","Las Alamandas Costalegre"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future"},{"si":"romance","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Cuixmala","posture":"Goldsmith ~25,000-acre private biosphere estate; suites/villas/casitas; zebras+turtles; private airstrip","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / luxury DMC (Journey Mexico) / villa specialist","virtuoso_value_add":"likely via luxury-DMC channel - verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision (private-airstrip clean-pass class)","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/mexico/cuixmala.html"},{"name":"Careyes (Casitas / Castles)","posture":"Brignone 1968 clifftop enclave; hotel + casitas + ~50 villas + moat-pool castles; polo/sailing/Ondalinda; private-air via Chamela CHM31 ~15 min","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / villa specialist","virtuoso_value_add":"verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://careyes.com/"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","posture":"Isabel Goldsmith 18-suite gated ultra-boutique on private bay; own 3,300-ft asphalt airstrip (currently unavailable - use Chamela strip 15 min)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"likely via luxury-DMC channel - verify","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/"},{"name":"El Careyes (Club & Residences)","posture":"beachfront club/residences arm of the Careyes enclave","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application","virtuoso_value_add":"verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://careyes.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Careyes (Costa Careyes), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.4,"lng":-105.03}}'::jsonb, 20),
  ('caye-caulker-belize', '10S', 'Caye Caulker', 'Belize', 'Caye Caulker Belize', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Belize', '{"tropical","liveaboard","expedition","ocean","culinary"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Car-free ~5-mi caye; golf carts + bikes only; national motto ''Go Slow''; reached by water taxi (~45 min from Belize City) or Tropic Air / Maya Island Air airstrip","The Split = channel hand-widened after Hurricane Hattie (1961), now ~100 ft deep; island''s social heart + Lazy Lizard bar","Snorkel/dive base for the Belize Barrier Reef (UNESCO); Hol Chan Marine Reserve US$15 park fee (Belize''s oldest marine park)","Value counterpoint to Ambergris - budget-to-comfort island; hotel ceiling is boutique (Iguana Reef Inn / Weezie''s), no branded ultra on-island","Ragga 3-day/2-night sail Caulker->Placencia via Blue Hole/reef (~US$400, chef, Tue/Fri); manatees at Swallow Caye Wildlife Sanctuary (10 BZD fee)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (verify locally)","hyperbaric_chamber":"NOT on Caye Caulker - nearest is San Pedro/Ambergris Caye (Belize''s only chamber, next to Ambergris Hope Clinic, 226-2660); Caulker dive-accident cases boated to San Pedro - factor transfer time","hospital":"small local clinic on-caye; serious trauma routes to Belize City hospitals by water taxi/air or air-evac; route around Southside Belize City","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; cayes open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE -> Caye Caulker (CUK) by Tropic Air / Maya Island Air puddle-jumper, or high-speed water taxi ~45 min; never touches Southside Belize City","the_split":"tidal current + boat traffic in the channel; not lifeguarded/boat-free; swim to sides, watch for boats, don''t swim impaired","malaria":"WHO-certified malaria-free (2023); a few mainland Cayo cases reappeared 2025; effectively none on the caye","dengue":"dengue/chikungunya/Zika active (daytime Aedes; Belize City cases up 2025) - DEET/picaridin, cover up","water":"tap water NOT potable - bottled/filtered only; mind ice/raw produce/unpasteurized dairy"},"timing":{"peak":"late-Dec-Apr (dry high season; Jan-Mar driest; Christmas-New Year + Easter sub-peaks)","dive_subpeak":"Mar-Jun (best viz, Blue Hole conditions)","shoulder_green":"Sep-Nov (green/rainy; Sep-Oct highest hurricane risk = value trough; late-Nov flips to dry comfort at low rates)","booking_window_lead_time":"value/short-lead market (weeks to a few months); 2-4 months for Dec-Apr peak + Christmas/Easter; book Blue Hole / 3-day Ragga sail ahead","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"dive/sail value packages, Lobsterfest tail, manatee + Goff''s Caye day trips, ''slow island at half price'', Nov dry-comfort-at-low-rates","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Easter, Lobsterfest (July), Independence season (Sep, overlaps hurricane risk)","fire_date":"peak: early-to-mid November (curve-start late-Nov minus 1-2 wks); dive/expedition: mid-February; green-value Nov push: late September; keep rolling last-minute layer year-round","flag":"value/short-lead market moves the curve faster than resort markets; Sep-Oct hurricane risk overlaps green window - sharpen on live booking-pace tracking","sources":["https://www.ashtoncourtbelize.com/blog/when-is-the-best-time-to-visit-caye-caulker.html","https://www.zubludiving.com/destination/belize/belize-district/ambergris-caye-san-pedro-caye-caulker","https://www.raggasailadventures.com/","https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/hotels-caye-caulker/"]},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"The Split + Lazy Lizard sunset swim","why":"hand-cut channel, crystal water, the island''s social heart at golden hour","timing":"year-round, best sunset","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caye_Caulker","si":"tropical","when":"year-round, best sunset","commission":"F&B/OTA-adjacent scene-setter, not a margin line"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Bike / golf-cart the car-free island","why":"the whole Go Slow experience in an afternoon","timing":"year-round","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.nomadicmatt.com/travel-guides/belize-travel-tips/caye-caulker/","si":"tropical","when":"year-round","commission":"local rental affiliate / DMC add-on"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Hol Chan Marine Reserve + Shark Ray Alley","why":"Belize''s oldest marine park; sharks/rays/turtles; US$15 fee","timing":"year-round, best viz Mar-Jun","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.backpackerswanderlust.com/caye-caulker-snorkeling-tours/","si":"liveaboard","when":"year-round, best viz Mar-Jun","commission":"local dive/snorkel operator + Viator/GYG affiliate; CLIA dive-lane convert to commissioned where offered"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Coral Gardens + seahorse stop","why":"shallow coral + seahorses on mangrove/grass roots - the caye''s signature soft moment","timing":"year-round","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/caye-caulker-l2496/caye-caulker-7-stop-snorkeling-in-the-belize-barrier-reef-t364340/","si":"liveaboard","when":"year-round","commission":"local operator + GYG affiliate"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Manatee + Goff''s Caye day tour (Swallow Caye Sanctuary)","why":"West Indian manatees in a protected sanctuary + sandbar-caye lunch","timing":"late-Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/swimming-with-manatees-belize/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"late-Dec-Apr","commission":"local operator + DMC + Viator affiliate (10 BZD sanctuary fee non-commissionable)"},{"si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures / Ocean Adventures","name":"Ragga 3-day sail to Blue Hole / Placencia","why":"sail the reef, camp on cayes, chef-cooked lobster on deck - the caye''s bucket-list expedition","timing":"year-round, Tue/Fri departures","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.raggasailadventures.com/","si":"Global Expedition Adventures / Ocean Adventures","when":"year-round, Tue/Fri departures","commission":"Ragga tour commission on application + dive-lane crossover"},{"si_tag":"ocean","name":"Sunset sailing cruise","why":"casual catamaran sundowner off the reef","timing":"year-round evenings","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.raggasailadventures.com/","si":"ocean","when":"year-round evenings","commission":"local operator + affiliate"},{"si_tag":"culinary","name":"Fry-jack breakfast + lobster season / Lobsterfest","why":"fried-dough island breakfast; July Lobsterfest; lobster in-season ~mid-Jun-mid-Feb","timing":"Lobsterfest July; lobster Jun-Feb","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.nomadicmatt.com/travel-guides/belize-travel-tips/caye-caulker/","si":"culinary","when":"Lobsterfest July; lobster Jun-Feb","commission":"F&B/event affiliate-adjacent"},{"si_tag":"ocean","name":"Kitesurfing off the reef flats","why":"steady trade-wind flats for kite","timing":"~Nov-Jun windier window","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.backpackerswanderlust.com/caye-caulker-snorkeling-tours/","si":"ocean","when":"~Nov-Jun windier window","commission":"local kite school + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do you get around Caye Caulker — do you need a car?","a":"No cars at all. The ~5-mile island runs on bikes (from ~15 BZD/day) and golf carts (~125–150 BZD/day) on sand streets, reached by high-speed water taxi (~45 min from Belize City) or small plane on the Tropic Air / Maya Island Air airstrip. The whole \"Go Slow\" experience is walkable and bikeable in an afternoon.","source":"nomadicmatt.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Caye Caulker good for snorkeling and diving?","a":"Yes — it is a value snorkel/dive base on the same Belize Barrier Reef as Ambergris. The Hol Chan Marine Reserve trip (US$15 park fee) puts you with sharks, rays and turtles in Belize''s oldest marine park; local operators run half-days ~US$50 and full-days ~US$90, with best visibility March–June.","source":"backpackerswanderlust.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can you sail to the Blue Hole from Caye Caulker?","a":"Yes — the Ragga 3-day/2-night sail (~US$400, Tuesday/Friday departures) runs Caulker to Placencia via the Blue Hole and reef, camping on tiny cayes with chef-cooked lobster on deck. Day options add manatees at Swallow Caye Wildlife Sanctuary (10 BZD sanctuary fee).","source":"raggasailadventures.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the food and lobster scene on Caye Caulker?","a":"Fry-jack breakfasts and beach BBQ anchor the everyday scene, and Lobsterfest lands in July as the island''s biggest food event. Lobster season itself runs roughly mid-June to mid-February, so a summer visit catches both the festival and fresh lobster.","source":"nomadicmatt.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on Caye Caulker?","a":"Two things: there is no recompression chamber on Caulker (nearest is San Pedro/Ambergris, so dive-accident cases are boated across — build in transfer time and carry DAN), and The Split is not a lifeguarded beach. The channel has tidal current and boat traffic, so swim to the sides, watch for boats, and don''t swim impaired at the Lazy Lizard. Hurricane risk peaks Sep–Oct.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving the Blue Hole from here dangerous?","a":"It is a deep dive (>100 ft) for experienced/advanced divers only — verify certification and operator briefing. Allow 18–24 hours before flying, because many guests leave BZE by puddle-jumper, and remember the nearest chamber is on Ambergris, so plan conservative profiles and factor the boat transfer time.","source":"zubludiving.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Caye Caulker Belize: The ''Go Slow'' Island Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel Hol Chan with sharks and rays, swim The Split at sunset, sail the Blue Hole — Caye Caulker is Belize''s car-free ''Go Slow'' caye and the value counterpoint to Ambergris. When, how, and how to stay safe.","slug":"caye-caulker-belize","primary_keyword":"Caye Caulker Belize","long_tail":["Caye Caulker Go Slow island","The Split Caye Caulker swimming","Caye Caulker snorkeling Hol Chan","Caye Caulker vs Ambergris Caye budget","how to get to Caye Caulker from Belize City","Raggamuffin Blue Hole 3-day sail","Caye Caulker where to stay budget"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Cayo Caulker Belice","bucear Cayo Caulker","snorkel Hol Chan Belice","cómo llegar a Cayo Caulker","hoteles económicos Cayo Caulker"],"hreflang":["en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Cayo Espanto","location":"private island 3 mi off San Pedro / Ambergris Caye","posture":"true branded ultra (nearest) - 7 villas incl. overwater Casa Ventanas, all-inclusive, houseman service, celebrity hideaway","price_tier":"ultra","rate_note":"~US$1,395-3,195/night meals incl., 4-night min","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso lane - commission on application","mor":"commissionable only where offered; no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.mrandmrssmith.com/luxury-hotels/cayo-espanto"},{"name":"Placencia peninsula (Itz''ana / Naia + peers)","location":"mainland-south Belize","posture":"alternate ultra/luxury base; 3-day Ragga sail ends near Placencia so Caulker+Placencia chain naturally","price_tier":"ultra/luxury","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso - on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.raggasailadventures.com/"},{"name":"Caye Caulker on-island","posture":"STRAIGHT: NO branded ultra on-caye; ceiling = comfortable boutique guesthouse (Iguana Reef Inn / Weezie''s); sell as day/character add to an Ambergris or Placencia ultra base","price_tier":"premier (ceiling)","earning":"n/a for ultra","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/hotels-caye-caulker/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Caye Caulker, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.7444,"lng":-88.025}}'::jsonb, 21),
  ('celestun-mexico', '10S', 'Celestún', 'Mexico', 'Winter estuary of the flamingos', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"expedition","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Ría Celestún Biosphere Reserve — west-coast flamingo estuary; 300+ bird species, crocodiles, sea turtles","Flamingos peak Nov-March, counts near 35,000 — opposite of Río Lagartos'' Apr-Sep peak","Ojo de Agua Baldiosera — largest freshwater spring in the mangrove, cenote-like swim stop; petrified forest + mangrove tunnels on tour","Boat tours ~1.5-2 hr, ~MXN 1,800-2,000 per boat (6-8 pax) from the pier/bridge","Closest flamingo coast to Mérida (~1.5-2 hr); remote for trauma — nearest full hospitals Mérida"],"safety":{"emergency_number":"911","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"nearest_trauma":"Mérida private hospitals (Star Médica, Clínica de Mérida, CMA, Faro del Mayab) ~1.5-2 hr; local clinic only in town","remote_flag":true,"activity_fires":["boat-safari life vests + CONANP-licensed operator","sun/dehydration open water","no-touch/no-flush wildlife","freshwater-spring swim (unlifeguarded)","remote medevac distance","mangrove/mosquito"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-10-27","peak":"Nov-March (best Dec-Feb, ~35,000 birds)","fire_date":"2026-10-13","shoulder":"Apr, Oct","green_offseason":"May-Sep (rainy, reduced counts — Río Lagartos takes over)","booking_lead_weeks":"3-6","notes":"Celestún flamingos peak Nov-March — OPPOSITE window to Río Lagartos (Apr-Sep). Follow-the-sun within Yucatán. Closest flamingo coast to Mérida (~1.5-2 hr). Sharpen on live tracking."},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Flamingo estuary tour (Ría Celestún)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.yucatan-wanderer.com/blog/the-complete-guide-to-visiting-celestun-and-its-flamingos","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC (Amstar) / GetYourGuide-Viator affiliate + non-commissionable reserve fee"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Ojo de Agua Baldiosera freshwater spring","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.posta.com.mx/yucatan/ojo-de-agua-baldiosera-una-maravilla-de-la-naturaleza-en-celestun-/v-vl2041855","timing":"Nov-March","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a cenote-like pool where swimming is possible, rising cold inside the salt estuary","si":"expedition","blurb":"a cenote-like pool where swimming is possible, rising cold inside the salt estuary","when":"Nov-March","commission":"bundled in boat tour"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Petrified forest (Bosque de Tampetén)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.turismomexico.es/yucatan/reserva-de-la-biosfera-ria-celestun/","timing":"Nov-March","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov-March","commission":"bundled in boat tour"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Mangrove tunnels","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.yucatan-wanderer.com/blog/the-complete-guide-to-visiting-celestun-and-its-flamingos","timing":"Nov-March","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov-March","commission":"bundled in boat tour"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Birding (300+ species)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.yucatan-wanderer.com/blog/the-complete-guide-to-visiting-celestun-and-its-flamingos","timing":"Nov-March","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov-March","commission":"specialist-guide referral / DMC"},{"si_tag":"Beaches/Romance","name":"Gulf beach + seafood cocteleria + quiet sunset","tier":"essential","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/celestun","si":"Beaches/Romance","commission":"content halo → dining/lodging affiliate + bedbank"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to see flamingos in Celestún?","a":"November through March, with December–February the sweet spot, because that is the winter mating congregation when as many as ~35,000 flamingos feed in the estuary — the exact opposite window from Río Lagartos'' April–September breeding peak. Counts swing year to year with rainfall, water level and salinity, so book the reserve and the season, not a promised number.","source":"yucatan-wanderer.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Celestún worth it as a beach or honeymoon add-on from Mérida?","a":"Yes, as a slow half-day-plus-beach pairing, not a resort. Celestún is the closest flamingo coast to Mérida at 1.5–2 hr by car, with a wide calm Gulf beach, waterfront seafood coctelería and crowd-free sunsets — the soft-romance counterpoint to a Mérida hacienda base. There is no all-inclusive layer here; it is small hotels and beach guesthouses.","source":"yucatan-wanderer.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What will I see beyond the flamingos?","a":"A full biosphere: 300+ bird species, crocodiles at the mangrove edge and sea turtles, plus the Ojo de Agua Baldiosera — the largest freshwater spring in the mangrove, a cenote-like swim stop rising cold inside the salt estuary — and the surreal petrified forest. Dedicated dawn birding is the draw once the Wildlife SI opens.","source":"yucatan-wanderer.com / posta.com.mx, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Celestún?","a":"Distance to trauma care, not crime. Celestún has only a basic local clinic; the nearest full-service private hospitals are in Mérida, 1.5–2 hr away by road — closer than Río Lagartos, but still not a place for time-critical injury. Build the medevac distance into risk expectations and carry travel-medical insurance.","source":"yucatanmagazine.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Celestún Flamingos & Biosphere: Estuary, Springs and Gulf Beach | TravelWell.World","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["flamencos Celestún","reserva de la biosfera Ría Celestún","tour flamencos Celestún desde Mérida","ojo de agua Baldiosera","bosque petrificado Celestún","Playa Norte Celestún"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","type":"Mérida luxury hacienda base (hub-and-spoke)","distance":"~25 min from Mérida; ~1.5-2 hr to Celestún","earning_lane":"Fora advisor lane","tier":"ULTRA","note":"No branded ultra in Celestún; luxury = hacienda base + private CONANP charter; tighter hub-and-spoke than Río Lagartos"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Celestún, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.8586,"lng":-90.3997}}'::jsonb, 22),
