ing":{"peak":"November–March snowbird/winter peak; near-perfect mild climate year-round","shoulder":"March–June (warmest, pre-rains, still comfortable)","green":"June–September/October summer rain (green, afternoon showers), value window","booking_lead":"Winter snowbird rentals/villas book months ahead (tight Ajijic housing); summer short-window","off_season_specials":"Green-season wellness value; disclose afternoon showers","event_peaks":"Snowbird winter influx Nov–Mar; year-round mild-climate base","campaign_start":"Snowbird/senior + wellness campaigns by late summer/early fall for Nov–Mar peak; green-season value by late spring"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ajijic yoga + spa + natural-health day","si_tag":"Wellness & Spa","status":"future","hook":"Lakeside yoga studios, spas, natural-health centers — restorative core","bookable_category":"spa/wellness bookings + classes","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.expatinsurance.com/articles/retiring-in-lake-chapala-mexico (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","blurb":"Lakeside yoga studios, spas, natural-health centers — restorative core","when":"year-round","commission":"wellness/spa affiliate + boutique-hotel spa","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Donaire Hotel Boutique spa","si_tag":"Wellness & Spa","status":"future","hook":"Full-service spa: deep-tissue, prenatal, couples treatment rooms","bookable_category":"spa + stay","tier":"premier","source":"https://casablancaajijic.com/best-boutique-hotels-in-ajijic/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","blurb":"Full-service spa: deep-tissue, prenatal, couples treatment rooms","when":"year-round","commission":"boutique-hotel / MoR","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Ajijic murals + galleries walk","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Pueblo Mágico art walk — murals, expat galleries, artisan shops","bookable_category":"guided art/culture walk","tier":"essential","source":"https://ajijicpueblomagico.mx/en/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–March snowbird/winter peak","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Pueblo Mágico art walk — murals, expat galleries, artisan shops","when":"November–March snowbird/winter peak","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Chapala malecón + gardens","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Historic municipal lakeside promenade, gardens, traditional-Mexican feel","bookable_category":"free / bundle","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.accesslakechapala.com/guide/chapala-living/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"culture","blurb":"Historic municipal lakeside promenade, gardens, traditional-Mexican feel","commission":"bundle with dining/tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Ajijic malecón + pier restaurant","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Quieter lakeside promenade with a restaurant out on the pier","bookable_category":"free promenade + dining","tier":"essential","source":"https://tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g499405-d2300167-Reviews-Ajijic_Malecon-Ajijic.html (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–March snowbird/winter peak","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Quieter lakeside promenade with a restaurant out on the pier","when":"November–March snowbird/winter peak","commission":"dining affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Snowbird lakeside long-stay","si_tag":"Senior Travel","status":"future","hook":"Multi-week/month seasonal rental, English-speaking community, mild climate, GDL access","bookable_category":"seasonal villa/expat rental","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thelatinvestor.com/blogs/news/lake-chapala-expat-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–March snowbird/winter peak","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"senior","blurb":"Multi-week/month seasonal rental, English-speaking community, mild climate, GDL access","when":"November–March snowbird/winter peak","commission":"villa/rental MoR","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real way to stay in the safe zone?","a":"Arrive at Guadalajara (GDL) and take a direct pre-arranged transfer to the lakeside. The Level 3 restrictions apply to rural southern-Jalisco highway corridors (Fed. Hwy 110 and Hwy 80), not the lake; GDL is a carve-out and the ~45-minute transfer runs between two carve-out zones. Do not detour onto the restricted highways.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why is Lake Chapala''s climate considered one of the best in the world?","a":"Because it barely moves — 23–27°C (74–80°F) year-round, warmest March–June, with no harsh off-season. That mild, stable lakeside climate at ~1,560 m is the foundation of the yoga, spa and natural-health scene and the reason retirees describe it as \"near-perfect.\"","source":"expatinsurance.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"What is there to do in Ajijic?","a":"Walk the art. Ajijic is a designated Pueblo Mágico of cobblestone lanes, murals, galleries and artisan markets, with a lakeside malecón and a pier restaurant; Chapala''s historic malecón and gardens are the traditional-Mexican counterpoint ~45 minutes from GDL. Mornings are best for the gallery walk.","source":"ajijicpueblomagico.mx / mexicorelocationguide.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Lake Chapala good for retirees and snowbirds?","a":"It is the definitional destination for it. An estimated 15,000–20,000 North American retirees live here full-time in an English-speaking, North-American-standard-services community, with the November–March snowbird season the peak. Winter rentals book months ahead given tight Ajijic housing.","source":"thelatinvestor.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"senior"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lake Chapala & Ajijic Travel Guide — Expat Lakeside, Wellness & Pueblo Mágico | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Mexico''s largest lake and its biggest English-speaking expat community: Ajijic''s Pueblo Mágico murals and galleries, Chapala''s malecón, a near-perfect year-round climate, and lakeside wellness — 45 minutes from Guadalajara airport.","slug":"chapala-ajijic-mexico","primary_keyword":"Lake Chapala Ajijic travel guide","long_tail":["is Ajijic safe to visit 2026","Ajijic Pueblo Mágico things to do","Lake Chapala climate year-round","Chapala vs Ajijic","Lake Chapala expat retiree community","Ajijic boutique hotels and spas","Guadalajara to Ajijic transfer"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Ajijic","¿es seguro viajar a Ajijic?","Ajijic Pueblo Mágico","clima Lago de Chapala todo el año","malecón de Chapala","hoteles boutique Ajijic","cómo llegar de Guadalajara a Ajijic"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"senior","status":"future"}],"ultra":[],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Chapala & Ajijic (Lake Chapala), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.2939,"lng":-103.2586}}'::jsonb, 23),
  ('chichen-itza-mexico', '10S', 'Chichén Itzá', 'Mexico', 'Chichén Itzá', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"culture","expedition","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["UNESCO World Heritage Site + one of the New Seven Wonders; opens 8:00 AM, last entry 4 PM, closes 5 PM","Spring-equinox serpent-shadow (Kukulcan descending El Castillo) ~Mar 20-21, 4:30-5:10 PM; 8,400+ visitors 2026; autumn equinox ~Sep 22-23","Climbing El Castillo BANNED since 2008 (INAH); unauthorized climb fines ~55,760-278,800 MXN (~US$3,200-16,000) as of 2025","Cenote Ik Kil ~3 km away - ~60 m wide, ~40 m deep open sinkhole; entry ~250 MXN (520 w/ buffet); swim/snorkel, no lifeguard","Balankanche grotto - guided >1 km Maya-Toltec ritual cave, ~10 m descent; entrance to the underworld"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"rural zone; nearest trauma care Merida (~2 hr W, Star Medica/Clinica de Merida) or Cancun (~2 hr E, Hospiten/Amerimed) or air-evac","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"yes - MID Merida ~2 hr W or CUN Cancun ~2 hr E; Chichen sits between","heat":"PRIMARY RISK - large open shadeless site in intense Yucatan sun; go at 8:00 AM opening, carry 1.5-2 L water, sun hat + high SPF; heat exhaustion #1 incident risk; equinox afternoons = long standing in heat + crowds","cenote":"Ik Kil = swim/snorkel only, NO lifeguard; provided life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers/children); shower off sunscreen; steep wet stairs. Balankanche = guided dry-cave walk only, not a dive site","dive_no_fly":"Chichen NOT a scuba destination (Ik Kil/Balankanche are swim/walk). Nearest hyperbaric chambers on coast (SSS/DAN Cancun, Playa, Cozumel; SSS Merida) ~2+ hr away; DAN says nearest hospital first","malaria":"effectively none in tourist zone","dengue":"active in Yucatan 2026; chikungunya/Zika circulate - use repellent at grotto/cenote","water":"bottled/purified only","hurricane":"Jun-Nov","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late January (spring-equinox bed/tour demand hardens Jan-Feb for the ~Mar 20-21 window)","peak":"dry season Nov-Apr (Dec-Jan busiest w/ Riviera Maya high season); SPRING EQUINOX ~Mar 20-21 is the single event peak (8,400+ visitors 2026, shadow 4:30-5:10 PM)","fire_date":"2027-01-08 (curve-start minus 1-2 wks; fire the spring-equinox campaign before beds/early-entry sell out)","shoulder":"May + Oct; autumn equinox ~Sep 22-23 is a green-window mini-spike","green":"Jun-Sep (extreme heat/humidity, hurricane-season afternoon rain) - go at 8:00 AM opening; sell Ik Kil as heat counterweight","booking_lead":"day-trip/excursion days-to-weeks; EQUINOX exception - book beds + guided early entry months ahead (Jan-Feb) for March","off_season_specials":"green window: anchor Chichen as marquee day-trip inside a Merida hacienda-circuit or Valladolid Pueblo-Magico stay; push autumn equinox as crowd-lighter alt to March","event_peaks":"Spring equinox ~Mar 20-21 (#1); autumn equinox ~Sep 22-23 (#2); Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa; free-Sunday crowds (Mexican nationals/residents)","note":"sharpen on live tracking - confirm 2027 equinox date + exact shadow window + site event rules before firing","sources":["https://yucatanmagazine.com/chichen-itza-equinox/","https://www.exoticca.com/us/blog/witnessing-the-2026-spring-equinox-chichen-itza-teotihuacan-and-beyond/","https://chichenitzamexico.org/entrance-fee/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Dawn / 8:00 AM early entry to El Castillo","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"DMC early-entry tour + INAH/CULTUR entry","source":"https://chichenitzamexico.org/entrance-fee/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the ceremonial core empty and cool before the buses; the only way to photograph the Wonder without crowds or midday heat","si":"culture","blurb":"the ceremonial core empty and cool before the buses; the only way to photograph the Wonder without crowds or midday heat","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar/Olympus DMC + Viator affiliate (site fees non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Spring-equinox serpent-shadow (Kukulcán descending)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"equinox early-entry tour + beds booked Jan-Feb","source":"https://yucatanmagazine.com/chichen-itza-equinox/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the once-a-year engineered light-and-shadow spectacle, 4:30–5:10 PM ~Mar 20–21; the event peak","si":"culture","blurb":"the once-a-year engineered light-and-shadow spectacle, 4:30–5:10 PM ~Mar 20–21; the event peak","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + affiliate; base beds via bedbank/consortia"},{"name":"Evening Noches de Kukulcán light-and-sound show","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"evening ticket + guide (verify seasonal schedule)","source":"https://www.chichenitza.com/tickets","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"after-dark projection-mapping over the ruins, extends the day and the spend","si":"culture","blurb":"after-dark projection-mapping over the ruins, extends the day and the spend","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + affiliate"},{"name":"Yaxunáh community-Maya alternative","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"private community tour (Amigo Tours / Marriott Bonvoy activities)","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/yaxunah-a-community-run-paradise/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a living Maya community + quiet archaeological zone just south of Chichén; the responsible, crowd-free counter to the Wonder","si":"culture","blurb":"a living Maya community + quiet archaeological zone just south of Chichén; the responsible, crowd-free counter to the Wonder","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"private-tour DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Cenote Ik Kil swim","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"entry ~250 MXN + combo day tour","source":"https://cenotetickets.com/blog/en/cenote-ik-kil-entrance-fee-2025/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the iconic ~40 m emerald sinkhole 3 km from the ruins with vine curtains and waterfalls","si":"expedition","blurb":"the iconic ~40 m emerald sinkhole 3 km from the ruins with vine curtains and waterfalls","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Balankanché caves (guided grotto)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"entry + guided cave tour","source":"https://www.chichenitza.com/cenotes/ik-kil-cenote","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":">1 km underworld ritual cave with ancient Maya-Toltec offering chambers, a few km from the ruins — the archaeology-under-the-earth complement to the surface city","si":"expedition","blurb":">1 km underworld ritual cave with ancient Maya-Toltec offering chambers, a few km from the ruins — the archaeology-under-the-earth complement to the surface city","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + affiliate"},{"name":"Hacienda Chichén stay + Yaxkin Spa","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"FIT / consortia direct","source":"https://www.haciendachichen.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","commission":"host/Fora-Virtuoso where property participates; commission on application"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the equinox serpent-shadow and how do I see it?","a":"The spring equinox around March 20–21 is the peak, when seven triangles of light descend the north staircase of El Castillo between roughly 4:30 and 5:10 PM and Kukulcán appears to slither toward the stone serpent-head — the Maya engineered it more than a thousand years ago. It drew 8,400 people in 2026; the autumn equinox (~Sep 22–23) is the quieter alternative. Book beds and guided early entry in January–February.","source":"yucatanmagazine.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you still climb the pyramid at Chichén Itzá?","a":"No — climbing El Castillo has been banned since 2008 by INAH to protect the structure, and as of 2025 unauthorized climbing draws fines of roughly US$3,200–16,000. You photograph the Wonder from the plaza at the 8:00 AM opening, before the buses and the heat.","source":"chichenitza.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can beginners and kids swim Cenote Ik Kil?","a":"Yes — it is a surface swim, not a dive. Ik Kil is a ~40 m-deep open sinkhole 3 km from the ruins with provided life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers and children) and no lifeguard, so shower off sunscreen first and take the steep wet stairs carefully. Entry is 250 MXN.","source":"cenotetickets.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where do you actually stay at Chichén Itzá?","a":"On-site the market is thin but premium — two heritage hotels: Hacienda Chichén (a restored 16th-c. hacienda on a 200-ha private jungle reserve with the Yaxkin Maya-healing spa) and the adjacent Mayaland. Most travelers base at Valladolid (~40 min) or the Mérida hacienda circuit (~2 hr) and day-trip the ruins.","source":"haciendachichen.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Chichén Itzá?","a":"Extreme heat and sun, not crime. The ceremonial core is a large, open, shadeless site in intense Yucatán sun, and heat exhaustion is the #1 incident risk — enter at the 8:00 AM opening, carry 1.5–2 L of water per person, wear a sun hat and high SPF, and plan a midday exit. On equinox afternoons you stand in heat among thousands, so hydrate and hold position early.","source":"exoticca.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How far is medical care from Chichén Itzá?","a":"Roughly 2 hours either direction — the zone is rural. The nearest full trauma care is Mérida (~2 hr west, Star Médica / Clínica de Mérida) or Cancún (~2 hr east, Hospiten / Amerimed), so carry travel-medical and evacuation insurance.","source":"chichenitzamexico.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Chichén Itzá 2026: Equinox Serpent Shadow, Ik Kil & Fees","meta_description":"Chichén Itzá is a New Wonder — see the spring-equinox serpent shadow (~Mar 20–21), swim Cenote Ik Kil and explore Balankanché caves. Fees (~697 MXN), hours, no-climb rule, safety.","slug":"chichen-itza-mexico","primary_keyword":"Chichén Itzá","long_tail":["Chichén Itzá spring equinox 2026 serpent shadow","Chichén Itzá entrance fee 2026","can you climb Chichén Itzá El Castillo","Cenote Ik Kil near Chichén Itzá","Balankanché caves","Hacienda Chichén heritage stay","Chichén Itzá day trip from Cancún Mérida"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Chichén Itzá equinoccio","serpiente de luz Kukulcán El Castillo","precio entrada Chichén Itzá 2026","no se puede subir El Castillo","Cenote Ik Kil Chichén Itzá","grutas de Balankanché","Chichén Itzá desde Cancún Mérida","Hacienda Chichén hospedaje"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hacienda Chichen Resort & Yaxkin Spa","tier":"premier-luxury boutique heritage (straight - extraordinary location/story, not 5-star palace)","why":"sleep at the foot of the Wonder; restored 16th-c. hacienda, 200-ha private jungle reserve, Maya-healing spa","earning":"FIT/consortia (Fora/Virtuoso where property participates), commission on application","mor":"host MoR on base-stay + private-tour side; site fees non-commissionable","source":"https://www.haciendachichen.com/"},{"name":"Chable Yucatan (Merida circuit, ~2 hr W) - nearest TRUE ultra","tier":"ultra-luxury (Leading Hotels of the World)","why":"200-yr San Antonio hacienda, 750 acres, spa beside a sacred cenote, ~30 min from MID; base for private-guided Chichen ultra day excursion","earning":"FIT/consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay + private tour","source":"https://www.lhw.com/hotel/Chable-Yucatan-Chochola-Merida-Mexico"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Chichén Itzá, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.6843,"lng":-88.5678}}'::jsonb, 24),
