cipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"type":"inland archaeological day-trip - no overnight lodging market; based from Tulum/Playa","peak":"Nov-Apr dry season (fewer mosquitoes, less heat/humidity); April standout; Dec-Jan busier (Riviera Maya high season)","shoulder":"May + Oct","green":"Jun-Sep (jungle heat/humidity peak, hurricane-season afternoon rain) - go at 8:00 AM opening","demand_driver":"Nohoch Mul climb REOPENED Dec 8, 2025 (42 m, groups of 15, 15-min limit, closed-toe shoes); VERIFY still open at booking","booking_window_lead_time":"day-trip/excursion booking (days to weeks); no overnight market; bed-night lead time sits on the Tulum/Playa base","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"N/A on-site (no beds); anchor Coba day trip to a coastal Tulum/Playa/Riviera Maya stay; sell cave-cenote swims as heat counterweight","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa (arrive 8:00 AM); post-reopening Nohoch Mul climb demand","campaign_start_trigger":"fire inside the coastal booking cycle (Aug-Oct winter peak; Feb-Mar shoulder); lead with ''Nohoch Mul is climbable again''","sources":["https://www.besttime2travel.com/coba","https://www.chichenitza.com/blog/nohoch-mul-the-tallest-temple-in-coba","https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/coba-ruins-guide/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Nohoch Mul pyramid climb","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"INAH entry + guided ruins tour","source":"https://www.chichenitza.com/blog/nohoch-mul-the-tallest-temple-in-coba","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the tallest Maya pyramids, reopened Dec 2025 via protective wooden staircase; jungle-canopy summit view","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the tallest Maya pyramids, reopened Dec 2025 via protective wooden staircase; jungle-canopy summit view","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"Amstar/Olympus DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Coba archaeological zone by bike/pedicab","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"guided tour + on-site bike/pedicab rental","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/coba-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"sprawling jungle Maya city linked by ancient white sacbé roads; cover it by bicycle or pedicab","si":"expedition","blurb":"sprawling jungle Maya city linked by ancient white sacbé roads; cover it by bicycle or pedicab","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Choo-Ha cave cenote","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"cenote entry + combo tour","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/coba-cenotes/","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"shallow, stalactite-filled cavern; the gentlest of the three — good family/first-cenote swim","si":"family","blurb":"shallow, stalactite-filled cavern; the gentlest of the three — good family/first-cenote swim","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Tankach-Ha cave cenote","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"cenote entry + combo tour","source":"https://www.mexicocenotesandruins.com/cenote-tankach-ha-coba/","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep cavern with 5 m & 10 m jump platforms and dramatic stalactites","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep cavern with 5 m & 10 m jump platforms and dramatic stalactites","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Multun-Ha cave cenote","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"cenote entry + combo tour","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/coba-cenotes/","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the third, quieter cave cenote in the Cobá cluster; cool clear underground pool","si":"expedition","blurb":"the third, quieter cave cenote in the Cobá cluster; cool clear underground pool","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Cobá?","a":"Heat and hydration, plus mosquitoes — not crime. Cobá is open, humid jungle with a 42 m pyramid climb, so the main risk is heat exhaustion: go at the 8:00 AM opening, carry ample water and sun protection. Dengue is active — Quintana Roo is among Mexico''s highest-activity states in 2026 — so use repellent; there is effectively no malaria.","source":"nomadoc.com.mx / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Can you climb Nohoch Mul in 2026?","a":"Yes — climbing reopened on December 8, 2025 after roughly six years closed, so verify it is still open at booking. A new wooden staircase now protects the original 120 stone steps up to the 42 m (138 ft) summit, one of the tallest Maya pyramids, with a jungle-canopy view from the top. Climb window is 8:00 AM–3:30 PM.","source":"chichenitza.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do you get around Cobá, and how far is it from the coast?","a":"By bicycle or pedicab — the site is too vast to walk comfortably. Cobá sits ~47 km (29 mi) NW of Tulum, so it is almost always done as a guided day trip from a Tulum, Playa del Carmen or Riviera Maya base; it has essentially no overnight lodging market of its own. The zone opens at 8:00 AM.","source":"xamanhaconnections.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Are the Cobá cenotes good for kids?","a":"Yes — the cave cenotes make an ideal cool-off after the ruins. Choo-Ha is shallow and gentle, the best first cenote for children; all three have safety ropes and provided life jackets. Shower off sunscreen before entering to protect the water, and take the steep, wet stone stairs carefully (Tankach-Ha is ~83 steps down).","source":"bucketlistbri.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Cobá?","a":"November–April, the dry season, is best — fewer mosquitoes, lower humidity and less heat for the jungle climb, with April the standout month. Whatever the season, arrive at the 8:00 AM opening to beat both the heat and the crowds; the June–September green season brings peak jungle heat and hurricane-season afternoon rain.","source":"besttime2travel.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cobá Ruins & Cenotes: Climb Nohoch Mul","meta_description":"Cobá is inland Maya jungle — climb the 42 m Nohoch Mul pyramid (reopened Dec 2025) and swim the Choo-Ha, Tankach-Ha and Multun-Ha cave cenotes. When, fees and safety.","slug":"coba-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cobá ruins","long_tail":["Nohoch Mul climbing 2026","Coba cenotes Choo-Ha Tankach-Ha","Coba ruins from Tulum","tallest Maya pyramid Quintana Roo","Coba bike pedicab jungle ruins"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["ruinas de Cobá","subir Nohoch Mul Cobá reabierto","pirámide más alta maya Quintana Roo","cenotes Cobá Choo-Ha Tankach-Ha Multun-Ha","Cobá desde Tulum","tour Cobá y cenotes","bicicleta bicitaxi ruinas de Cobá"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"family","status":"future"}],"ultra":[],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cobá, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.495,"lng":-87.736}}'::jsonb, 26),
  ('colchagua-valley-chile', '10S', 'Colchagua Valley & Chilean Wine Country', 'Chile', 'Colchagua Valley & Chilean Wine Country', 'live', 'verified', 'restaurant', 'Santiago & Central Valley Wine', '{"culinary","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"131","emergency_all":{"ambulance":"131","fire":"132","police":"133"},"advisory_level":"L2","advisory_reissued":"2026-05-20","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"via Santiago SCL, ~2-3 hr drive to Santa Cruz","key_safety_line":"drink-driving — always use a designated driver or guided wine tour","trauma_pathway":"Santa Cruz / San Fernando clinics -> Santiago evac (~2-3 hr)","water":"potable","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-08-18T23:18:12+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak_windows":["Fiesta de la Vendimia — March 6-8, 2026 (Santa Cruz)","Autumn/harvest — March-May","Spring — October-November","Summer — December-February"],"inflection":["late February (pre-Vendimia climb)","late September (spring travel)"],"trough":"winter June-August (off-season fill)","fire_date":"2026-02-15 (mid-February — curve-start minus 1-2 weeks, ahead of Vendimia)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Viña Montes feng-shui cellar (Apalta)","si_tag":"Culinary/Wine","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.wanderlustchloe.com/top-places-to-go-wine-tasting-in-the-colchagua-valley-vina-montes/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Built in 2004 on feng-shui principles; wooden path over a lagoon, 800 oak barrels in a semicircle serenaded by Gregorian chant","si":"Culinary/Wine","blurb":"Built in 2004 on feng-shui principles; wooden path over a lagoon, 800 oak barrels in a semicircle serenaded by Gregorian chant","when":"year-round","commission":"estate visit + lunch via DMC/AOR"},{"name":"Lapostolle / Clos Apalta biodynamic winery","si_tag":"Culinary/Wine","tier":"luxury","source":"https://southamericawineguide.com/winery/lapostolle-clos-apalta-winery/","si":"Culinary/Wine","commission":"premium tasting + lunch via AOR"},{"name":"Viu Manent horse-drawn carriage (century-old Malbec)","si_tag":"Culinary/Wine","tier":"comfort","source":"https://viumanent.cl/en/visitenos/tour-degustacion/tour-en-carruaje/","hook":"Family winery, wine-tourism pioneer since 1995; carriage or e-bike rides through the San Carlos vineyard where vines top 100 years","si":"Culinary/Wine","blurb":"Family winery, wine-tourism pioneer since 1995; carriage or e-bike rides through the San Carlos vineyard where vines top 100 years","commission":"tour+tasting+lunch via DMC/AOR"},{"name":"Carmenère vertical tasting","si_tag":"Culinary/Wine","tier":"premier","source":"https://southamericawineguide.com/winery/lapostolle-clos-apalta-winery/","hook":"A multi-vintage Carmenère flight at Lapostolle or Montes — the grape''s Chilean redemption story in a glass","si":"Culinary/Wine","blurb":"A multi-vintage Carmenère flight at Lapostolle or Montes — the grape''s Chilean redemption story in a glass","commission":"premium tasting upsell via AOR"},{"name":"Colchagua Wine Train (Tren del Vino)","si_tag":"Culture/Heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.welcomechile.com/rancagua/wine-train.html","hook":"Antique rail cars — a 1913 coal-fired steam engine among the last built in Chile","si":"culture","blurb":"Antique rail cars — a 1913 coal-fired steam engine among the last built in Chile","commission":"packaged full-day tour via DMC"},{"name":"Santa Cruz Plaza + Museo de Colchagua","si_tag":"Culture/Heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thetravelmavens.com/riding-chiles-wine-train-to-the-colchagua-valley.html","hook":"The Colchagua Museum is the largest private collection in Chile","si":"culture","blurb":"The Colchagua Museum is the largest private collection in Chile","commission":"museum non-commissionable; hotel via AOR/bedbank"},{"name":"Harvest grape-stomp (Fiesta de la Vendimia, March)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.cavacolchagua.cl/en/2026/02/19/vendimia-de-colchagua-2026/","hook":"Roll up the sleeves and stomp grapes in wooden vats amid parades and plaza music — a once-a-year, deeply photogenic couple''s experience","si":"romance","blurb":"Roll up the sleeves and stomp grapes in wooden vats amid parades and plaza music — a once-a-year, deeply photogenic couple''s experience","commission":"Vendimia-timed lodge package via AOR"},{"name":"Vineyard cycling loop (Santa Cruz radius)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://talesfromthelens.com/cycling-wine-tasting-colchagua-valley-chile/","hook":"Four to five quality wineries within 10 km, bikes under ~€7/24h — a self-paced tasting loop on two wheels","si":"expedition","blurb":"Four to five quality wineries within 10 km, bikes under ~€7/24h — a self-paced tasting loop on two wheels","commission":"bike rental + guided cycling day via DMC"},{"name":"Dawn hot-air balloon over the vines","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://produncan.cl/en/discover-santa-cruz-the-heart-of-the-colchagua-valley/","hook":"Panoramic valley flight ending in a wine toast and breakfast","si":"expedition","blurb":"Panoramic valley flight ending in a wine toast and breakfast","commission":"operator booking via DMC/AOR"},{"name":"Horseback ride through the vineyards","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.andbeyond.com/places-to-stay/south-america/chile/wine-country/vik-hotel/","hook":"Estate rides at Viu Manent, Vik, and Clos Apalta Residence across vines and foothills","si":"expedition","blurb":"Estate rides at Viu Manent, Vik, and Clos Apalta Residence across vines and foothills","commission":"estate experience or lodge inclusion via AOR"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Colchagua for wine?","a":"March to May (autumn) is the named ideal window for wine tourism, because harvest activity, color on the vines, and comfortable temperatures line up together. The signature event is the Fiesta de la Vendimia in Santa Cruz, which in 2026 runs March 6, 7, and 8 — the single highest-demand window, so book far ahead.","source":"colchaguawinetours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Colchagua good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — the load-bearing draw here is wine-estate lodging built for two. Clos Apalta Residence puts 10 lodgings on a 1,235-acre reserve with full board, and adjacent Viña Vik offers 22 titanium-clad suites over a lagoon, both with fireplaces, private terraces, and paired estate wines. A honeymoon here is deliberately slow.","source":"relaischateaux.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you cycle between the wineries?","a":"Yes, and it''s the valley''s signature soft-adventure. Bikes rent for under about €7 per 24 hours, and four to five quality wineries sit within a 10 km radius of Santa Cruz, making a self-paced tasting loop feasible in daylight — provided the rider driving stays untasted, wears a helmet, and carries water.","source":"talesfromthelens.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the single biggest safety risk in Colchagua?","a":"Drink-driving — this is the defining operational rule. Tastings run all day, so never self-drive between wineries; use a designated driver or a guided wine tour, which is illegal to skip above Chile''s low BAC limit. Local clinics in Santa Cruz and San Fernando stabilize; serious cases evacuate to Santiago, roughly 2–3 hours away.","source":"colchaguawinetours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the hot-air balloon and horseback add-ons dangerous?","a":"Low risk when booked right — both are guided by definition. Dawn balloon flights (e.g., Heu''Tour) are weather-dependent, so fly only with a licensed, insured operator and confirm the cancellation-for-wind policy; estate horseback rides use helmets and guides. Confirm travel-medical and evac coverage first, since serious cases evacuate to Santiago (~2–3 hr); ambulance is 131.","source":"produncan.cl, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"search_language":"es-CL","meta_title":"Colchagua Valley, Chile — Wine Country Travel Guide (Santa Cruz, Apalta & the Wineries) | TravelWell.World","local_keywords":["Valle de Colchagua viñas","ruta del vino Colchagua","Vendimia Santa Cruz","viña Montes Apalta","tren del vino Colchagua","Museo de Colchagua","Carménère Colchagua"],"hreflang":["en","es-CL"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Colchagua Valley & Chilean Wine Country"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culinary","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Clos Apalta Residence","affiliation":"Relais & Châteaux","earning":"advisor commission on FIT + full-board; Fora/Virtuoso-eligible via R&C","mor":"hotel/host","tier":"$$$$$"},{"name":"Viña Vik","affiliation":"Relais & Châteaux (Millahue, adjacent)","earning":"advisor commission; R&C / luxury-consortia eligible","mor":"hotel/host","tier":"$$$$$"},{"name":"Noi Blend Colchagua","affiliation":"boutique-luxury","earning":"advisor commission on FIT; consortia-adjacent","mor":"host/hotel","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Colchagua Valley & Chilean Wine Country, Chile"},"geo":{"lat":-34.6413,"lng":-71.366}}'::jsonb, 27),
  ('colonia-del-sacramento-uruguay', '10S', 'Colonia del Sacramento, Uruguay', 'Uruguay', 'Portuguese cobblestones, a lighthouse over the river, Buenos Aires', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Montevideo & The Atlantic Coast', '{"culture","romance","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_updated":"2025-05-07","advisory_reason":"crime (property + some violent) concentrated in Montevideo, Canelones, Maldonado, Rivera — not Colonia","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Montevideo Carrasco (MVD) + ~2.5-hr road transfer, or Buenos Aires day-ferry ~1–3 hr (Buquebus / Colonia Express)","ferry_border_flag":"BA↔Colonia is an Argentina→Uruguay international crossing — clear immigration at terminal, arrive 1.5–2 hr early, passport required","trauma":"local Colonia clinic/hospital for routine + stabilization; severe trauma escalates by road (~2.5 hr) to Montevideo + international evac; carry medical/evac insurance","crime_note":"Colonia reads calm vs. Montevideo national profile; standard small-town care in ferry-terminal crush + after dark","cobblestone_footing":"uneven 300-yr cobbles, slick when wet — closed gripped footwear; most common minor injury","water":"potable","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uruguay","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2025-12-10T13:00:39+00:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"summer Dec–Feb (~27 °C days) + spring/fall shoulders (Sep–Nov, Mar–May, ~15–22 °C)","inflection":"Buenos Aires attach — Colonia demand rides the BA/Montevideo curve; thin overnight inventory + summer ferry seats fill early","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1–2 weeks — early–mid Nov for summer; ~2 wks ahead of shoulder start; highest-yield = fire on the traveler''s confirmed BA/Montevideo dates","off_season_fill":"winter Jun–Aug (~8–15 °C) — slow-travel romance overnights + Carmelo indoor-cellar wine day"},"jewels":[{"name":"Barrio Histórico + Calle de los Suspiros (12-block UNESCO quarter)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/things-to-do-in-colonia-del-sacramento-uruguay/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided walk DMC 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%; museum ticket non-commissionable"},{"name":"The Lighthouse (Faro, 111 steps) + Portón de Campo city gate","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/uruguay/colonia-del-sacramento-guide-uruguay/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"guided-walk anchor DMC 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%; lighthouse entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Plaza de Toros Real de San Carlos (restored 1910 bullring, reopened 2022)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attractions-g298066-Activities-Colonia_del_Sacramento_Colonia_Department.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / guided circuit 10–20%"},{"name":"Vintage-car photo circuit","si_tag":"culture_heritage+romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.guruguay.com/colonia-del-sacramento/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Colonia''s antique cars sit like sculpture on old-town corners; a curated photo/heritage-drive circuit is a natural romance+heritage crossover experience","si":"culture_heritage+romance","blurb":"Colonia''s antique cars sit like sculpture on old-town corners; a curated photo/heritage-drive circuit is a natural romance+heritage crossover experience","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"DMC / private-guide add-on 10–20%"},{"name":"Sunset on the Rambla Costanera","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/uruguay/colonia-del-sacramento-guide-uruguay/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Colonia''s boardwalk fronts sandy beaches and small colonial homes rather than high-rises","si":"romance","blurb":"Colonia''s boardwalk fronts sandy beaches and small colonial homes rather than high-rises","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"content anchor — drives boutique-hotel + dining revenue"},{"name":"The overnight after the ferry leaves (converted-casona boutique)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/uruguay/colonia-del-sacramento-guide-uruguay/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"boutique bedbank 10–18% / consortia"},{"name":"Buenos Aires day-ferry framing (romantic day-escape / overnight)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/buenos-aires-l1/buenos-aires-to-colonia-tours-t314607/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"ferry package / affiliate 4–10%"},{"name":"Carmelo Tannat wine day — Narbona + Bodega Cordano","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://matadornetwork.com/read/uruguay-wine-country/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the ~80 km up-river wine sub-region built on Tannat, Uruguay''s national grape. Narbona","si":"culinary","blurb":"the ~80 km up-river wine sub-region built on Tannat, Uruguay''s national grape. Narbona","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"DMC/guided wine day w/ transport 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is there to do in Colonia del Sacramento''s Barrio Histórico?","a":"You can cover Colonia''s UNESCO Barrio Histórico on foot in about 4–5 hours including lunch: walk the ~12-block grid, the 1700s-era Calle de los Suspiros, the Plaza Mayor house-museums, and the Portón de Campo drawbridge gate, then climb the 111-step lighthouse for river-and-town views. It is compact because the Portuguese laid it out in 1680.","source":"guruguay.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Colonia worth an overnight, or just a day trip?","a":"Worth the overnight — that is the town''s quiet secret. Most travelers arrive on the day-ferry from Buenos Aires, so staying a night gives you the emptied cobbles at dusk and dawn and a sunset on the Rambla as the Río de la Plata turns copper. Book ahead: the top boutique, Charco, has only 8 rooms.","source":"cuppatocopatravels.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you do a wine day from Colonia del Sacramento?","a":"Yes — the wine day runs ~80 km up-river to Carmelo, Uruguay''s Tannat sub-region, with estate lunches at Narbona (a 1909-founded estate) and Bodega Cordano. Book it guided or with a driver: the fire to plan around is drink-and-drive on rural roads.","source":"matadornetwork.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Colonia?","a":"Footing, not crime. The single most common visitor injury is a twist or fall on the Barrio Histórico''s uneven 300-year-old cobbles, which turn slick in the wet. Wear closed, gripped footwear and take extra care in rain and after dark — unguided walking is otherwise fine. Tap water is potable, and 911 is the nationwide emergency line.","source":"guruguay.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Do I need my passport for the Buenos Aires day-ferry?","a":"Yes — the crossing is an Argentina→Uruguay international border, and it is the single most common trip-planning error. Passengers clear immigration and customs at the terminal before boarding and check-in closes early, so arrive 1.5–2 hours before departure with your passport for both legs.","source":"directferries.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Colonia del Sacramento, Uruguay — UNESCO Barrio Histórico, the Lighthouse & a Carmelo Wine Day | TravelWell","search_language":"es-UY","local_keywords":["Colonia del Sacramento qué hacer","Barrio Histórico Colonia","Carmelo bodegas","ferry Buenos Aires Colonia","Calle de los Suspiros","Faro de Colonia del Sacramento","Tannat Uruguay","Rambla Colonia atardecer"],"hreflang":["en","es-UY"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Narbona Wine Lodge","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Carmelo (~80 km / ~1 hr from Colonia)","product":"5-room ultra-boutique estate, king rooms + private terraces, pool, winery, restaurant, Puerto Camacho boat access","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Carmelo Resort & Spa","brand":"Hyatt Unbound Collection","area":"Carmelo (~1 hr from Colonia)","product":"44 keys incl. 24 bi-level suites + 20 detached villas, spa, tennis, indoor pool","earning":"Hyatt Privé / consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Charco Hotel","area":"Barrio Histórico, Colonia (riverfront, ~10-min walk from ferry port)","product":"8-room design boutique in converted original 1680 Portuguese houses, on-site restaurant + patio","earning":"consortia (Fora/Virtuoso where listed) + bedbank premium; MoR via consortium/bedbank","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Colonia del Sacramento, Uruguay, Uruguay"},"geo":{"lat":-34.4718,"lng":-57.8446}}'::jsonb, 28),
  ('costalegre-mexico', '10S', 'Costalegre (Costa Alegre)', 'Mexico', 'Costalegre Mexico', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"tropical","romance","ultra","ocean"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["~200 mi undeveloped Pacific coast between Puerto Vallarta and Manzanillo; PV->Barra de Navidad ~4-hr drive on Hwy 200","Five littoral areas: Bahia de Chamela, Costa Careyes, Cuixmala, Bahia de Tenacatita, Bahia de Navidad","Chamela-Cuixmala Biosphere Reserve ~32,000 acres tropical dry forest; UNAM research station since 1971","Humpback whales migrate Dec-Mar; Chamela islands (Isla Cocinas/Pajarera) reachable by boat","Ultra enclaves Careyes, Cuixmala, Las Alamandas with private airstrips; Chalacatepec airport completed Mar 2024 (operational status pending)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"remote coast; serious cases route to Manzanillo (~1.5 hr from Careyes area) or Puerto Vallarta (~2-4 hr north); carry travel-medical + air-evac insurance","advisory_level":"L3","book_enabled":false,"tourist_zone_carveout":"none (southern Jalisco coast NOT a named carve-out)","air_access_verified":"Manzanillo (ZLO, Colima) / PVR - not into a named carve-out; new Chalacatepec airport planned (verify); private airstrips at Careyes/Cuixmala/Las Alamandas - founder-review flag","founder_flag":"private-airstrip ''resort-airstrip private-access'' clean-pass class - flag for founder review; content-only until founder rules on carve-out","malaria":"low - mosquito avoidance (not prophylaxis) for Jalisco coastal lowlands below 1,000 m","dengue":"circulates (Jalisco cases 2025; peak May-Nov) - daytime repellent","water":"drink bottled/purified","hurricane":"May-Nov - trip insurance for summer/fall","remote":"limited services between towns; carry water/fuel/meds; do NOT drive secondary roads after dark (advisory warning)","road_transfer":"transfers pass through non-carve-out southern Jalis