DO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season, calm, humpbacks Dec-Mar, Careyes polo/events season, ultra-villa demand highest)","shoulder":"May & late Oct (warm, quieter, pre/post rains)","green":"Jul-Oct (hot/humid, emerald hills, hurricane window May-Nov, softer rates)","event_peak":"Careyes polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","booking_window_lead_time":"ultra villas for Christmas-New Year/winter holidays book 6-12 months ahead, contracted direct on application; green-season windows far shorter","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green season (Jul-Oct) eco/wildlife (turtle nesting, biosphere), sportfishing, storm-quiet villa buyouts at softer rates - the ''secret season''","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year (ultra premium), Semana Santa/Easter (Agua Alta Cup polo), Ondalinda (mid-Nov), winter polo season","campaign_start_trigger":"content-only - no campaign; if founder rules carve-out for private-airstrip enclaves, open winter/holiday villa campaigns in spring for following Nov-Apr peak (6-12-mo lead)","sources":["https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/","https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","https://www.costalegre.ca/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Careyes clifftop Castles & Iconic Villas","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"staffed clifftop villas with moat-like infinity pools; Heidi Klum married here, celebrities vacation here","si":"ultra","blurb":"staffed clifftop villas with moat-like infinity pools; Heidi Klum married here, celebrities vacation here","when":"year-round","commission":"on application / villa specialist"},{"name":"Cuixmala (Casa Cuixmala suites / hillside villas)","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Cuixmala direct / luxury DMC","source":"https://cuixmala.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre reserve estate — zebras, nesting turtles, total seclusion","si":"ultra","blurb":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre reserve estate — zebras, nesting turtles, total seclusion","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Las Alamandas direct / DMC","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"18 suites across 8 villas, gated ultra-boutique. On application","si":"ultra","blurb":"18 suites across 8 villas, gated ultra-boutique. On application","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Chamela Bay islands (Isla Cocinas / Isla Pajarera)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"local panga boat tour (content-only)","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"local operator (n/a while content-only)"},{"name":"Tenacatita Bay","si_tag":"Tropical Islands","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"local operators (content-only)","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"is famed for clear water, snorkeling, kayaking and paddleboarding; Chamela Bay is dotted with marine-reserve islands reachable by boat tour","si":"tropical","blurb":"is famed for clear water, snorkeling, kayaking and paddleboarding; Chamela Bay is dotted with marine-reserve islands reachable by boat tour","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"local (content-only)"},{"name":"Barra de Navidad lagoon village","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"Grand Isla Navidad Resort / boutique (content-only)","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/barra-de-navidad-mexico/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"colonial-shipyard fishing town with a scenic lagoon and slow small-town charm — an authentic couples'' base","si":"romance","blurb":"colonial-shipyard fishing town with a scenic lagoon and slow small-town charm — an authentic couples'' base","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"OTA/DMC (content-only for the coast)"},{"name":"Winter humpback whale coast (Dec-Mar)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"local whale/boat tour (content-only)","source":"https://www.costalegre.ca/","si":"ocean","commission":"local operator (content-only)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book Costalegre through TravelWell right now?","a":"No — it is content-only. Jalisco sits at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (May 29, 2026), and the advisory''s four named no-restriction carve-outs (Guadalajara Metro, Puerto Vallarta, Chapala, Ajijic) do not include the southern-Jalisco Costalegre coast, so book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on Costalegre?","a":"The road transfer, and the remoteness. Ground access runs through non-carve-out southern Jalisco on Highway 200 and secondary roads, and the advisory warns against secondary highways after dark — the hold reason. The coast is remote: serious cases route ~1.5 hr to Manzanillo or 2–4 hr to Puerto Vallarta, so air-evac insurance is essential.","source":"travel.state.gov / lprluxury.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What makes Costalegre a true ultra coast?","a":"Three private enclaves with their own airstrips. Careyes (clifftop castles + ~50 staffed villas), Cuixmala (a ~25,000-acre Goldsmith biosphere estate) and Las Alamandas (an 18-suite gated boutique) form one of Mexico''s most private ultra nodes — the private-air arrival is the crux of a possible future clean-pass.","source":"cuixmala.com / careyes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ultra"},{"q":"What are the best beaches and islands here?","a":"Chamela Bay and Tenacatita. Chamela is dotted with marine-reserve islets (Isla Cocinas, Isla Pajarera) reachable by panga, and Tenacatita (~30 min north of Barra de Navidad) is famed for clear, calm water for snorkel, kayak and SUP — the calmest bays on a ~200-mile coast.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"When can I see whales on Costalegre?","a":"December to March. Humpbacks migrate and breach offshore along the whole coast in the dry winter season — the same window as peak ultra-villa demand — while the Chamela–Cuixmala biosphere adds turtle nesting and dry-forest wildlife. Keep a regulated distance on any boat tour.","source":"costalegre.ca, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Costalegre Mexico: Careyes, Cuixmala & the Wild Jalisco Coast","meta_description":"Costalegre — ~200 mi of undeveloped Jalisco Pacific coast between Puerto Vallarta and Manzanillo: Careyes, Cuixmala, Las Alamandas, Tenacatita, Barra de Navidad. Ultra villas, whales, biosphere.","slug":"costalegre-mexico","primary_keyword":"Costalegre Mexico","long_tail":["Costalegre luxury villas","Careyes Cuixmala Las Alamandas","Costalegre vs Puerto Vallarta","Tenacatita Bay snorkeling","Barra de Navidad travel guide","Costalegre whale watching Dec-Mar"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Costalegre Jalisco","villas de lujo Careyes","Cuixmala reserva biosfera","Las Alamandas Costalegre","Bahia Tenacatita snorkel","Barra de Navidad que hacer","avistamiento de ballenas Costalegre"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"future"},{"si":"romance","status":"future"},{"si":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Cuixmala","posture":"Goldsmith ~25,000-acre biosphere estate; suites/villas/casitas; private airstrip","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / luxury DMC (Journey Mexico) / villa specialist","virtuoso_value_add":"likely via luxury-DMC channel - verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision (private-airstrip clean-pass class)","source":"https://cuixmala.com/"},{"name":"Careyes (Casitas / Villas / Castles)","posture":"Brignone 1968 enclave; hotel + casitas + ~50 villas + clifftop castles; polo/sailing/Ondalinda; private-air (Chamela strip ~15 min / Chalacatepec ~40 min)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / villa specialist","virtuoso_value_add":"verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://careyes.com/"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","posture":"Isabel Goldsmith 18-suite gated ultra-boutique on private bay; own 3,300-ft airstrip (currently unavailable - use Chamela strip 15 min)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"likely via luxury-DMC channel - verify","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/"},{"name":"El Careyes (Club & Residences)","posture":"beachfront club/residences arm of Careyes enclave","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application","virtuoso_value_add":"verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://careyes.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Costalegre (Costa Alegre), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.44,"lng":-105.04}}'::jsonb, 29),
  ('cozumel-mexico', '10S', 'Cozumel', 'Mexico', 'Cozumel drift diving', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"diveglobal","liveaboard","ocean"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Reefs sit on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef (Great Mayan Reef); drift diving averages ~1.5 knots","Signature walls: Palancar (accessible), Santa Rosa (expert), Columbia Deep","Parque Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel reef bracelet = MX$220 (~US$13) per person per day (Jan 2026)","Multiple recompression chambers on-island: SSS/Int''l Hospital + Costamed (DAN preferred provider)","Banco Chinchorro (largest W-hemisphere atoll) is ~30-35 nm off Costa Maya, launched from Xcalak/Mahahual - NOT Cozumel"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Costamed / Cozumel International / Medica San Miguel / General Hospital (town); serious trauma to Cancun private hospitals or US air-evac","recompression_chambers":[{"name":"SSS Recompression Chamber / Medicina Hiperbarica Integral","address":"Calle 5 Sur #21-B, Centro, Cozumel QR 77600","phone":"+52 (987) 872-1430 / 872-2387","emergency_24h":"(987) 103-5524","network":"IDAN Referral Center / UHMS / EUBS"},{"name":"Costamed Hyperbaric Center (Cozumel Medical Center)","opened":"Nov 2013","network":"DAN Recompression Chamber Network Preferred Provider"}],"dan_emergency":"+1-919-684-9111","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"extremely low / none in tourist zone","dengue":"active - Quintana Roo among highest-activity states 2026; chikungunya/Zika also circulate","water":"bottled/purified only","hurricane":"Jun-Nov (peak Aug-Oct)","dive_no_fly":"12h single / 18h multi-day / 24h deco (DAN); use 24h conservative given repetitive day-boat profiles","drift_diving":"briefing required; SMB; dive within cert; Santa Rosa Wall expert-only","chinchorro":"no chamber at atoll; nearest chambers hours away on mainland/Cozumel - extra-conservative profiles + DAN cover","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Mar (calmest seas, clearest skies, 200ft+ viz; Dec24-Jan1 crowded/expensive spike)","shoulder":"Nov (~25-40% off Dec) and May (~20-30% off April); near-peak conditions","green":"May-Sep warmest water ~27-28C / calmest seas; summer humidity + hurricane risk Jun-Nov (peak Aug-Oct)","booking_window_lead_time":"peak dive weeks book well ahead; Chinchorro multi-day + private crewed dive-yacht = book months ahead (limited weather windows / small vessels)","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green-summer value story: warmest/calmest water + 20-40% off rooms, thinner crowds, pair with hurricane trip insurance","holiday_event_peaks":["Cozumel Carnival 2026: main parades Feb 14/15/17 (Fat Tue), run Feb 11-18, pre-Carnival Jan 17-Feb 8; floats with pre-Lenten lunar calendar","cruise-ship day-crowds congest San Miguel + nearer reefs — push early boats / south-zone sites"],"campaign_start_trigger":"open peak-season campaign Aug-Sep for Dec-Mar; shoulder push Sep-Oct (Nov) and Feb-Mar (May); Carnival micro-campaign Nov-Dec for mid-Feb"},"jewels":[{"name":"Palancar Reef (Gardens/Caves/Bricks/Horseshoe)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"2-tank day-boat dive","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","commission":"dive-op DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Santa Rosa Wall","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive (expert-only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC"},{"name":"Columbia Deep","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive","tier":"comfort","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC"},{"name":"Banco Chinchorro atoll","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"future","bookable":"multi-day/liveaboard-style from Xcalak/Mahahual","tier":"premier","source":"http://www.pelagiclife.org/chinchorro","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"Aggressor/liveaboard reseller = Commissioned Agent on application"},{"name":"Palancar snorkel + El Cielo sandbar","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","bookable":"catamaran/snorkel tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","si":"ocean","blurb":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","commission":"Viator/GYG affiliate + DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cozumel?","a":"Decompression discipline, not crime — this is a repetitive multi-day dive island. Follow DAN''s no-fly windows strictly (12h single, 18h multi-day, 24h conservative), because Cozumel''s day-boat profiles stack dives fast; the island has multiple chambers, but a bad no-fly call is the classic mistake. Also plan for dengue (repellent), bottled water and hurricane season (Jun–Nov).","source":"dan.org / travel.state.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is drift diving in Cozumel dangerous?","a":"No, when you take the drift briefing seriously — but it is not passive. Expect a near-constant ~1.5-knot current that does the swimming for you; do a controlled descent, stay with the group and dive master, deploy an SMB, and dive within your certification. Santa Rosa Wall is expert-only; Palancar Gardens suits most certified divers.","source":"cozumelscuba.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the best dive sites in Cozumel, and can beginners dive them?","a":"Palancar Gardens is the everyone-friendly classic — coral pinnacles, archways and swim-throughs at 100-ft-plus visibility with mild current — while Santa Rosa Wall and Columbia Deep are advanced drifts. Beginners and newly certified divers do best at Palancar; Santa Rosa, dropping from ~15 m into the blue, is expert-only.","source":"torntackies.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I do a liveaboard from Cozumel?","a":"Not from Cozumel itself — it is a day-boat island. True liveaboard-style multi-day diving goes to Banco Chinchorro, ~30–35 nm off Costa Maya, launched from Xcalak or Mahahual to the south, not Cozumel. The luxury alternative near Cozumel is a private crewed dive-yacht charter, since overnight liveaboards are effectively banned inside the national park.","source":"pelagiclife.org / islandlifemexico.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can non-divers snorkel Cozumel, and what''s the reef fee?","a":"Yes — the reef is superb for snorkelers, from Palancar shallows to the El Cielo starfish sandbar by catamaran. Everyone entering the marine park pays the reef bracelet, MX$220 (~US$13) per person per day as of Jan 2026; snorkel tours carry no no-fly restriction, making them a good last-day option before a flight.","source":"cozumelmio.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is Cozumel good for a honeymoon or a couples'' dive trip?","a":"Yes — it pairs world-class diving with real staffed villas. Luxury Cozumel and Villa Experience run oceanfront staffed homes (chef, concierge) from ~US$450/night, and there is no branded ultra flag on-island, so for hotel-brand luxury couples ferry to Mayakoba (Rosewood, Banyan Tree) ~an hour away.","source":"luxurycozumel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Cozumel?","a":"December–March is peak, with the calmest seas, clearest skies and legendary 200-ft-plus visibility. November and May are the value sweet spots — near-peak conditions at ~25–40% (Nov) and ~20–30% (May) below Dec rates; May–September brings the warmest, calmest water (~27–28°C) but summer humidity and hurricane risk.","source":"sunsetcozumel.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cozumel Diving: Drift the Mesoamerican Reef","meta_description":"Cozumel is the Caribbean''s drift-diving crown - Palancar, Santa Rosa Wall and the Mesoamerican Reef, with chambers, no-fly rules and the Chinchorro liveaboard hook.","slug":"cozumel-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cozumel drift diving","long_tail":["Cozumel dive sites Palancar Santa Rosa","Cozumel marine park fee 2026","Banco Chinchorro liveaboard","Cozumel recompression chamber","Mesoamerican Barrier Reef diving"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["buceo en Cozumel","arrecife Palancar Santa Rosa","camara hiperbarica Cozumel","buceo de deriva Cozumel","Parque Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel","Banco Chinchorro buceo","villa privada de lujo Cozumel"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"liveaboard","status":"future","note":"Cozumel = day-boat reef diving; liveaboard/multi-day runs to Banco Chinchorro launch from Xcalak/Mahahual, NOT Cozumel"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private Paradise Villa","location":"Cozumel (on-island)","what":"oceanfront exclusive-use villa, sleeps up to 24, 40+ staff incl. 7 rotating chefs + British-butler-trained butlers","why_ultra":"full-buyout fully-staffed private-resort — the on-island ultra expression","earning":"villa-agency/DMC commission on application (agent-of-record; no net-rate resale)","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a standalone; attach Virtuoso mainland stay for perks","mor_posture":"clean agent-side; red-flag any villa-inventory mark-up","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://privateparadisevilla.com/"},{"name":"Private crewed dive-yacht charter","location":"Cozumel / Riviera Maya (on-water)","what":"fully-crewed private yacht (captain+deckhand+dive master, chef/hostess on premium boats), 15+ sites + El Cielo, premium open bar","why_ultra":"ultra dive expression; only luxury ''liveaboard-style'' the park''s vessel-size rules allow (overnight liveaboards effectively banned in-park)","earning":"charter/DMC commission on application","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a direct; pair with Virtuoso stay","mor_posture":"agent-of-record on charter; no net-rate resale","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://dayyachtcharters.com/cozumel-yacht-charters-luxury-boat-rentals.html"},{"name":"Riviera Maya branded ultra (Rosewood/Banyan Tree Mayakoba, Chable Maroma, Maroma Belmond)","location":"Riviera Maya mainland (ferry + short transfer)","what":"Forbes/branded ultra-luxury resorts + villas; private pools, top spas, PGA course","why_ultra":"nearest true branded ultra flag — no ultra flag on Cozumel itself","earning":"Virtuoso preferred rate + commission (or via host-Virtuoso)","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade, daily breakfast for two, early check-in/late check-out, ~US$100 credit, VIP welcome (Mayakoba flags)","mor_posture":"standard Virtuoso agent-of-record","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/mayakoba-riviera-maya"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cozumel, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.423,"lng":-86.9223}}'::jsonb, 30),
  ('cuenca-ecuador', '10S', 'Cuenca & the Southern Andes, Ecuador', 'Ecuador', 'Cuenca & the Southern Andes', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Andes (Quito) & Galápagos', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"Cuenca — Mariscal Lamar (CUE), domestic-only, via Quito (UIO) / Guayaquil (GYE)","altitude_m":{"cuenca":2560,"el_cajas_toreadora":3960,"el_cajas_max":4450,"ingapirca":3150},"altitude_rule":"Mild AMS at Cuenca (~2,560 m) — slow first day, hydrate 3+ L/day, easy on alcohol; do El Cajas (~4,000 m) after a day or two in the city","trauma":"Good expat-grade private clinics in Cuenca; escalate to Quito or evacuate to US; confirm air-evac insurance","urban_crime":"standard L2 petty-crime discipline in markets/terminals/festival crowds","water":"ETAPA tap treated to WHO standard; new arrivals use filtered/bottled first weeks","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Coastal Region FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabí Santa Elena Guayas El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabi Santa Elena El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except: airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"June–September (drier/sunniest) + secondary dry spell ~December","event_peak":"Cuenca Independence — Nov 3; Pase del Niño Viajero — Dec 24","inflection_curve_start":"mid-April–May (dry window); October (Independence)","fire_date":"late March–April (dry season); September–early October (Nov 3 / Dec 24 festivals)","green_offseason":"February–April (greenest, wettest, best value)","binding_constraint":"thin boutique-colonial inventory in historic center around festivals"},"jewels":[{"name":"Catedral de la Inmaculada Concepción (blue domes)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Cathedral_of_Cuenca","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Cuenca''s signature: three great domes tiled in blue-and-white glaze from old Czechoslovakia, Romanesque-Revival, built 1885 over nearly a century","si":"culture","blurb":"Cuenca''s signature: three great domes tiled in blue-and-white glaze from old Czechoslovakia, Romanesque-Revival, built 1885 over nearly a century","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC city walking tour / activity affiliate"},{"name":"El Barranco + Río Tomebamba","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://trans-americas.com/city-travel-guide-cuenca-ecuador/","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The terraced river-edge where colonial houses spill down to the water, walking paths, cafés and the old-town/modern-city dividing line. Free to wander","si":"culture","blurb":"The terraced river-edge where colonial houses spill down to the water, walking paths, cafés and the old-town/modern-city dividing line. Free to wander","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC walking tour; boutique-hotel proximity"},{"name":"Homero Ortega Panama-hat workshop & museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/homero-ortega-workshop-and-museum","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"The living home of the sombrero de paja toquilla — a family museum + active toquilla-straw workshop + boutique","si":"culture","blurb":"The living home of the sombrero de paja toquilla — a family museum + active toquilla-straw workshop + boutique","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC craft tour + boutique retail"},{"name":"Ingapirca — largest Inca ruin (Temple of the Sun)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://happygringo.com/blog/ingapirca-ruins-ecuador/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"A rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun — the only one of its kind in the empire","si":"culture","blurb":"A rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun — the only one of its kind in the empire","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC full-day guided or self-serve bus + site entry"},{"name":"Gualaceo & Chordeleg craft villages (silver filigree + ikat)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.cuencabestours.com/day-tours/gualaceo-and-chordeleg-craft-making-villages-tour","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC craft-circuit day tour + artisan retail"},{"name":"Museo Pumapungo","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumapungo_Museum","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Cuenca''s biggest museum — ethnographic + art collections and the Inca-era Pumapungo archaeological site/etno-botanical park on a hillock over the Tomebamba","si":"culture","blurb":"Cuenca''s biggest museum — ethnographic + art collections and the Inca-era Pumapungo archaeological site/etno-botanical park on a hillock over the Tomebamba","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC guided city/culture tour (entry free)"},{"name":"Mirador de Turi","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/ecuador/the-southern-highlands/cuenca/attractions/mirador-de-turi/a/poi-sig/436630/363371","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"The hilltop viewpoint over Cuenca''s colonial skyline — a chapel, restaurants and the classic photo, especially at sunset and during the Nov–Dec Christmas-lights season","si":"culture","blurb":"The hilltop viewpoint over Cuenca''s colonial skyline — a chapel, restaurants and the classic photo, especially at sunset and during the Nov–Dec Christmas-lights season","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC city tour; taxi/transfer"},{"name":"Cuenca festivals — Independence (Nov 3) & Pase del Niño (Dec 24)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.patrimoniocultural.gob.ec/pase-del-nino-viajero/","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A three-day civic festival and Azuay''s largest religious parade — the two dates that most enrich a heritage-focused trip","si":"culture","blurb":"A three-day civic festival and Azuay''s largest religious parade — the two dates that most enrich a heritage-focused trip","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"festival-timed lodging + DMC cultural programming"},{"name":"El Cajas National Park — Toreadora & páramo lakes (~3,960 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.moontravelguides.com/travel/outdoors/ecuadors-el-cajas-national-park/","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"28,000 ha, 786 lakes, wildflower páramo and rare polylepis stands","si":"expedition","blurb":"28,000 ha, 786 lakes, wildflower páramo and rare polylepis stands","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC/local guided hike or activity affiliate; park entry pass-through"},{"name":"Baños de Cuenca thermal circuit — Piedra de Agua","si_tag":"RHN / Wellness","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelwritingpro.com/piedra-de-agua-hot-springs-spa-banos-de-cuenca-ecuador/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Volcanic hot springs 20 min from downtown, water surfacing at ~75°C and cooled to a bathing 36–40°C","si":"RHN / Wellness","blurb":"Volcanic hot springs 20 min from downtown, water surfacing at ~75°C and cooled to a bathing 36–40°C","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / spa entry pass-through + transfer"}],"faq":[{"q":"What makes Cuenca a UNESCO World Heritage city?","a":"Its historic center is a living colonial grid crowned by the New Cathedral — the Catedral de la Inmaculada Concepción, whose three blue-and-white domes were tiled with glaze from old Czechoslovakia and whose towers were left truncated by a load-bearing miscalculation. Built from 1885 over nearly a century, it is free to enter, with dome access monetized.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture-&-heritage-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Ingapirca worth the day trip from Cuenca?","a":"Yes — it is Ecuador''s largest Inca ruin, ~80 km north (~3,150 m), a rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun, the only one of its kind in the empire, built atop a Cañari sacred rock. Go guided full-day (highest margin) or self-serve by Transportes Cañar bus (~$3.50).","source":"happygringo.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture-&-heritage-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Cuenca a good romantic honeymoon base?","a":"Yes — it is a gentle, walkable heritage-city honeymoon, not a beach one. Restored 19th-century casonas like Mansión Alcázar (three blocks from Parque Calderón, with garden, spa and fine dining) and Hotel Santa Lucía anchor the boutique-colonial base, with the Baños de Cuenca thermal circuit — water surfacing at ~75°C — 20 minutes out.","source":"travelwritingpro.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you hike El Cajas from Cuenca on your own?","a":"Only partly — go guided beyond the marked loops. El Cajas (28,000 ha, 786 lakes) has no cell signal and weather that turns in minutes; only the Laguna Toreadora and Laguna Llaviucu loops are well marked, and exposure deaths have occurred on unmarked trails. The ~2-hour Toreadora loop (~3,960 m) is self-guided-feasible for the acclimatized.","source":"moontravelguides.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cuenca?","a":"Altitude, not crime. Cuenca sits at ~2,560 m, just above the 2,500 m AMS threshold — effects are usually mild and pass in 2–3 days — but El Cajas hiking at ~3,960–4,000 m is genuine high-altitude exertion. Take a slow first day, hydrate 3+ L/day, skip alcohol early, and do Cajas after a day or two in the city rather than on arrival.","source":"mytrip2ecuador.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is El Cajas dangerous?","a":"It can be if you go off-trail unprepared — exposure deaths have occurred there. The park has no cell signal and weather changes in minutes; only the Toreadora and Llaviucu loops are well marked. Guided is strongly preferred beyond those two loops; carry layers, a rain shell, water and food regardless of forecast, and hike after acclimatizing.","source":"moontravelguides.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes, Ecuador — Travel Guide, El Cajas, Ingapirca & Panama Hats | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Cuenca Ecuador","Parque Nacional Cajas","Ingapirca","ruinas de Ingapirca desde Cuenca","sombrero de paja toquilla Cuenca","Gualaceo Chordeleg artesanías","Catedral Nueva de Cuenca cúpulas azules","Baños de Cuenca aguas termales","Pase del Niño Viajero","Independencia de Cuenca 3 de noviembre"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Mansión Alcázar","location":"Cuenca historic center","earning":"Fora/Virtuoso where preferred; agency AoR + amenities","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$–$$$$"},{"name":"Hotel Santa Lucía","location":"Cuenca Old Town","earning":"agency AoR; Fora/Virtuoso if preferred","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Casa del Águila","location":"Cuenca","earning":"agency AoR; affiliate","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Hacienda stays (Azuay/Cañar countryside)","location":"outside Cuenca toward craft villages/Ingapirca","earning":"MoR / agency","mor":"agency/MoR","tier":"$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-2.9005,"lng":-79.0045}}'::jsonb, 31)
